      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\cos x$? Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The function is zero at $x=0.$\n- **II.** The complete set of inputs at which the function has maximum values is $x=\\frac{3\\pi}{2}+2n\\pi.$\n- **III.** The range of the function is $[-1,0].$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\cos x$.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186176047/assets/cosine.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. $\\cos(0)=1$.\n\n- Statement II is false. The maximum value is $1$, attained at $x=2n\\pi$. Every maximum input must be included.\n\n- Statement III is false. The minimum value is $-1$ and the maximum value is $1$. The range is $[-1,1]$.",
